From fab61b2fee237323833be3fa333054ce669fbff5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dameng <dameng@local>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 01:15:13 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] EDBT v4 B4: replayable query-submission schedule
 (--schedule_seed)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

An explicit query set does NOT fix Shuffled submission order — the
permutation stream comes from std::random_device. --schedule_seed <n>
(Shuffled mode only, enforced) replaces it with a seeded mt19937. Because
the dispatch loop is single-threaded and counter-driven, submission i
maps to perm_{floor(i/n)}[i mod n] regardless of how the concurrent
clients interleave: same seed + same item set replays the same schedule
(up to the run's own length; completion ORDER stays free and is visible
in the per-item results JSON).

When set, the runner writes next to the JSON output:
- <json>_schedule_plan.csv: header (seed,item_count,plan_length=100000)
  + pre-simulated plan from a private generator advancing in lockstep
  (initial shuffle + one shuffle per wrap; E4 phase switching not
  simulated — Phase B never enables it, warning printed if combined);
- <json>_schedule_manifest.csv: actual submissions
  (submission_index,item_id,item_name,scheduled_unix_ns).
schedule_seed is also recorded in the benchmark context JSON.

Verification (12s JOB runs, 10 clients, no plugin): seed=101 twice ->
plans byte-identical, manifests 553/553 rows prefix-identical and exact
prefixes of the plan; seed=202 diverges from submission 0.
